# known_consumers.list — the G8 reachability registry.
#
# Every KNOWN consumer of the catalog, one per line:
#   <consumer-name>\t<source>
# where <source> is:
#   local:<repo-relative pubspec path>     (our own integrator apps/examples)
#   github:<owner/repo>:<pubspec path>     (verified external adopters)
#
# WHY (the 2026-07-04 vision-alignment audit): landing is not reception. The
# unit published 0.4.x while its ONE verified adopter pinned ^0.3.0 and its
# OWN reference app pinned ^0.3.0 — nobody could receive what we built, and
# no loom measured it. G8 asks, at every publish: "which known consumer pins
# actually receive this release?" A LEFT-BEHIND consumer demands an explicit
# serve-decision (lift the pin / backport / recorded restraint) — never
# silence.
#
# Add a line whenever a real consumer is verified (downstream-pull sensor,
# adoption ledger, or a maintainer telling us). Remove only with a ledger note.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2026-07-31 — THE COHORT THAT ACTUALLY TRAVELS.
#
# Until now this registry knew three rows, and none of them was a PUBLISHED
# package that carries a pin on the catalog into a stranger's resolve. The
# first-party packages that DO travel — each published on pub.dev, each with a
# frozen pin a `pub add` consumer inherits — were invisible to the reach gate.
# The gate could therefore report a clean G8 while every real downstream pin
# excluded the release under test.
#
# Every pin below was MEASURED from that package's own pubspec on 2026-07-31,
# and cross-checked against the FROZEN pin in its latest published archive via
# the pub.dev API (`latest.pubspec.dependencies`). Both agreed for all seven.
#
# HONEST BOUND, load-bearing: the `local:` scheme reads this WORKING TREE's
# pubspec, not the frozen published one. They coincide today (verified above);
# if a working-tree pin is edited ahead of a republish, G8 will read the edited
# pin and report reach the published cohort does not actually have. The registry
# schema has no "published archive" source to point at. Stated, not silently
# passed.
#
# Measured pins vs the staged condition_aggregator 0.1.0 (published latest 0.0.8):
#   condition_aggregator_jma           ^0.0.5   (published 0.3.1)
#   condition_aggregator_nws           ^0.0.5   (published 0.0.7)
#   condition_aggregator_digitraffic   ^0.0.5   (published 0.0.6)
#   condition_aggregator_met_norway    ^0.0.5   (published 0.0.5)
#   condition_aggregator_owm_road_risk ^0.0.5   (published 0.1.4)  <-- not in the round-6 brief; found by measuring
#   driving_weather                    ^0.0.5   (published 0.5.0)  <-- not in the round-6 brief; found by measuring
#   drive_situation_fusion             ^0.0.7   (published 0.1.0)
# Dart's caret on a 0.0.x base is >=0.0.5 <0.1.0 (pub_semver nextBreaking
# increments the MINOR while major is 0 — MEASURED against the real solver, not
# recalled: a probe pinning ^0.0.5 resolved to 0.0.8). So all seven admit the
# published 0.0.8 and all seven EXCLUDE a 0.1.0. The serve-decision that follows
# is the Chair's, not this file's.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
example-app	local:example/pubspec.yaml
jitreq-drunkenv2	github:Jitreq/drunkenv2:pubspec.yaml
sngnav-app	github:aki1770-del/sngnav-app:pubspec.yaml
condition_aggregator_jma	local:packages/condition_aggregator_jma/pubspec.yaml
condition_aggregator_nws	local:packages/condition_aggregator_nws/pubspec.yaml
condition_aggregator_digitraffic	local:packages/condition_aggregator_digitraffic/pubspec.yaml
condition_aggregator_met_norway	local:packages/condition_aggregator_met_norway/pubspec.yaml
condition_aggregator_owm_road_risk	local:packages/condition_aggregator_owm_road_risk/pubspec.yaml
driving_weather	local:packages/driving_weather/pubspec.yaml
drive_situation_fusion	local:packages/drive_situation_fusion/pubspec.yaml
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROW ANNOTATIONS — history is annotated, never deleted.
#
# example-app  (local:example/pubspec.yaml)
#   CONFIRMED NO-DEP on condition_aggregator, 2026-07-31. It reaches the package
#   ONLY through `dependency_overrides:` (a path override to ../packages/
#   condition_aggregator); its `dependencies:` section carries no such entry.
#   reach_gate reads the `dependencies:` section only, by design, so this row
#   correctly reports NO-DEP. A path override is a monorepo convenience — it is
#   NOT reach, and must never be counted as a consumer receiving a release.
#
# jitreq-drunkenv2  (github:Jitreq/drunkenv2:pubspec.yaml)
#   *** UNVERIFIED — the source no longer exists. NOT confirmed NO-DEP. ***
#   Measured 2026-07-31: raw.githubusercontent.com/Jitreq/drunkenv2/HEAD/
#   pubspec.yaml -> HTTP 404, and api.github.com/repos/Jitreq/drunkenv2 ->
#   HTTP 404 "Not Found". The repo is deleted, renamed, or now private.
#   The round-6 brief asked us to confirm this consumer "does NOT depend on
#   condition_aggregator at all". That CANNOT be confirmed: the artefact needed
#   to answer it is gone. A dead verifier renders UNVERIFIED, never *cleared*
#   (OPS-069(A)) — so the row stays, carrying its honest state, rather than
#   being quietly retired into a NO-DEP that was never measured.
#   This matters beyond bookkeeping: drunkenv2 is recorded as the unit's FIRST
#   verified external adoption (0->1, 2026-06-21, pinning ^0.3.0). Whether that
#   adopter still exists is a REACH question for PDS/the Chair, not a registry
#   edit. Until then G8 reports it GONE and stays red.
#
# sngnav-app  (github:aki1770-del/sngnav-app:pubspec.yaml)
#   REACHABLE (HTTP 200, 2026-07-31) and it DOES depend on the catalog:
#     condition_aggregator: '>=0.0.3 <0.1.0'   (a range, not a caret)
#     condition_aggregator_jma: ^0.3.0
#   The range's own upper bound excludes a 0.1.0. Recorded here so the row is
#   read as measured fact, not inferred from the package name.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
